{"id":"e08ece86-a36e-4b46-943f-d69534b27f15","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.041","title":"Paleogenomics illuminates mobility and changing lifeways in Chalcolithic Anatolia","title_zh":"古基因组学揭示西铜石器时代安纳托利亚的人口迁移与生活方式转变","doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.041","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.041","abstract":"Once labeled the \"Dark Ages\" of Anatolian prehistory, the Chalcolithic period (c. 6000-3000 BCE) was characterized by drastically reduced settlement densities compared with the preceding Neolithic and the succeeding Bronze Ages, a change interpreted as population decline. Using 44 new genomes combined with published data, we find no evidence for a population reduction. The genetic evidence instead suggests that populations in Chalcolithic Anatolia were increasingly mobile and/or growing in size while receiving gene flow from eastern regions (e.g., East Anatolia and the South Caucasus) through a 3,000-year-long admixture process. We propose that genetic and archaeological evidence may be reconciled by hypothesizing the presence of communities with dispersed and mobile lifeways that are mostly invisible to archaeology. These communities also practiced consanguinity at frequencies unobserved in previous periods. Finally, we identify a mid-5th-millennium BCE individual in Central Anatolia carrying ∼10%-30% Pontic-Caspian Steppe-related ancestry, shedding light on mobility between the Eurasian Steppe and Anatolia.","abstract_zh":"西铜石器时代（约公元前6000-3000年）曾被称为安纳托利亚史前史的“黑暗时代”，其定居点密度远低于此前的新石器时代和随后的青铜时代，这一现象被解释为人口下降。利用44个新基因组及已发表数据，我们发现人口减少的证据不足。相反，遗传证据表明，西铜石器时代的安纳托利亚人口在接收来自东部地区（如东安纳托利亚和南高加索）的基因流的同时，日益流动和/或规模增长，这一混血过程持续了约3000年。我们假设，存在以考古学难以察觉的分散且流动方式生活的社群，从而可以协调遗传与考古学证据。这些社群的近亲婚配频率在以前时期均未出现。最后，我们在中安纳托利亚发现一名中新石器时代（中纪元5千纪）个体，携带约10%-30%的黑海-里海草原相关血统，揭示了欧亚草原与安纳托利亚之间的人口迁移情况。","snippet":"Once labeled the \"Dark Ages\" of Anatolian prehistory, the Chalcolithic period (c. 6000-3000 BCE) was characterized by drastically reduced settlement densities compared with the